TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Final Report (Part 2): Space Mission Design","overview":"Develop a preliminary space-mission design that benefits Australia and report the mission concept and its space-segment elements. Use mission-design software of your choice, supported by hand calculations if useful, and justify the proposed design."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Introduction: mission concept and rationale. Include the following required information: What is the spacecraft's primary mission? Why is the mission needed? How many spacecraft are used and why? Who are the users (operator and customers)?","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Addresses all requirements to a high standard. Detailed descriptions and discussions are included. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Addresses some requirements. Descriptions may feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Many or all requirements are not addressed. Poor descriptions or lack of appropriate referencing."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Main body: mission design. Present a summary of the mission design using software and/or hand calculations as appropriate. Include relevant screenshots and software files in the main body of the report and/or appendix. Include the following information: Where will it launch from, and using which launch vehicle? Why did you choose this option? What type of orbit will you use? What are its characteristics and orbital elements? Will you need to perform any orbital maneuvers? Which ground control facilities will you use? How often will your spacecraft be able to communicate with ground control? How long will the mission last, and what are your plans for EOL?","weight":60,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Demonstrates high level understanding of the design procedure. Design clearly addresses mission and course concepts. Major requirements are all addressed and are well supported with quality evidence (e.g. software screenshots, software files, hand calculations, references from literature). Content is comprehensive, accurate, and persuasive."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Demonstrates adequate understanding of the design procedure. Design may be inconsistent with regards to purpose and clarity of thought or feature errors. Major requirements are addressed but may lack some detail or are not well supported with evidence. Content may not be comprehensive and/or persuasive."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Demonstrates minimal understanding of the design procedure. Major requirements are not addressed and/or lack evidence. Content is incomplete or not persuasive."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Conclusion","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Detailed and appropriate conclusions reached from the evidence provided in the report."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Some conclusions are reached but they may be generic or lack specific detail."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful conclusions reached."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical engineering report structure. The report is easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Executive summary (or abstract) provides a concise overview of the report. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design - Launch"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design - Orbit (COE table)"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design - Orbit"},{"id":"R7","met":"yes","where":"Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R8","met":"yes","where":"Mission Duration & EOL"},{"id":"R9","met":"yes","where":"Ground Control & Communications (STK)"},{"id":"R10","met":"partial","where":"Screenshots provided (Images 1-5, access report) but no explicit STK files or appendix mentioned"},{"id":"R11","met":"partial","where":"Structure and citations present, but Wikipedia cited and reference formatting poor"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Design - Orbit","issue":"Contradictory statement: 'A very high altitude would yield low resolution images which is also desirable' – low resolution is not desirable; likely a missing negation."},{"where":"Bibliography [6]","issue":"Wikipedia used as a source, explicitly not acceptable per task requirements."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","issue":"Redundant/contradictory reasoning: uncontrolled descent considered then dismissed because satellite 'is without thrust capability', which was already stated; drag sail discussion incomplete sentence."},{"where":"Mission Design - Orbit","issue":"Inclination-vs-altitude plot (Image 3) provenance unclear – appears reproduced without clear citation or shown hand calculation; RAAN=27.33° justified only loosely as launch-site location."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"Claim that vertical inclination 'maintains a significant contact for the vast majority of passes' is imprecise; contact geometry not quantified beyond STK output."}],"overall":"A well-structured, comprehensive mission design addressing nearly all requirements with genuine STK evidence and a sensible SSO/ground-station choice. Weakened by referencing flaws (Wikipedia), missing figure/table numbering, a few technical contradictions, and no explicit software files or hand calculations.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"All required elements addressed: primary mission (fluid-lensing reef monitoring), rationale with cited bleaching statistics, single-spacecraft justification, and users/funding. Detail is good with references, though user discussion is brief and operator/customer roles could be more explicit.","evidence":[{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Coral reefs, specifically the Great Barrier Reef, would immensely benefit from dedicated satellite monitoring."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Thus, only one satellite is required."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"The proposed satellite would likely be used by governmental and science agencies (e.g. CSIRO, BOM)"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":42.0,"max":60.0,"reasoning":"All major requirements addressed: launch site/vehicle with justification, SSO with COE table (a=6971km, i=97.79° correct for 600km SSO), manoeuvres, ground station with STK access report, duration and EOL. Weakened by the altitude/resolution contradiction, unclear provenance of the inclination plot, no hand calculations shown, and no explicit STK files/appendix.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Design - Launch","quote":"The proposed satellite will thus use the Vega E rocket as a launch vehicle – launched from the Guiana Space Centre Spaceport."},{"where":"Mission Design - Orbit","quote":"an altitude of 600km requires a mean inclination of 97.7924°"},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","quote":"Systems Tool Kit 11 (STK) was used to calculate access periods as seen below"},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","quote":"The most promising alternative is a ‘drag sail’"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":7.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Conclusions follow from the evidence and acknowledge design risks (Vega E availability, fallback to Vega C). Somewhat summary-like rather than drawing deeper engineering insights (e.g. coverage gaps, data latency), but specific and appropriate.","evidence":[{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"A specific launch vehicle – the Vega E – has been selected although it has not been built yet."},{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"The Mt Pleasant Radio Observatory is well-located to receive data from this orbit type constantly and for long durations."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":10.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear structure with headings and executive summary; in-text citations match list. However, figures/tables lack numbers, references are bare URLs with Wikipedia used (explicitly disallowed), and there are grammar/typo errors ('a Earth observation', 'complied', 'purposed', 'current owned'). Not professional-level presentation.","evidence":[{"where":"Bibliography","quote":"[6] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_spaceflight. [Online]."},{"where":"Orbit","quote":"STK 3D view of orbit: 12 hours apart"},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","quote":"This station is current owned and operated by the University of Tasmania"}]}]}
